{
  "format": "pinmame-harness-scenario",
  "version": 1,
  "game": "kpb105",
  "notes": "Capcom Kingpin C1.01 Switch Test walk on fresh isolated state. Inside the test the flipper buttons browse the ROM's switch list, so the first steps browse the cabinet entries 05-08 (flipper buttons, Start, coin door), which the menu navigation itself uses. Then each public switch 1-4 and 9-80 is held while the DMD names the closed switch with its ROM switch number, wire colours and connector pin, pairing the ROM's own switch number and name with the public address. Flipper buttons are pressed through PinMAME's flipper-column button bits (public 84 left, 82 right): kpb105 declares FLIP_SWNO(5,6), and with keyboard handling off core_updateSw copies those bits into matrix switches 5/6 every frame, so a direct host write to 5 or 6 lasts at most one frame.",
  "actions": [
